examples.question_text:
The bar chart shows a sampling distribution of $\bar{X}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=35mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\path[use as bounding box] (-2.7,-0.65) rectangle (6.4,0.52);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.2,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,0.48);
\foreach \y in {0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4} {
\draw (-0.08,\y)--(0,\y);
\path (-0.08,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};
}
\path (-0.08,0) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\foreach \x/\v/\p in {1/2/0.1,2/4/0.2,3/6/0.4,4/8/0.2,5/10/0.1} {
\draw (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\p);
\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
}
\path (3,-0.45) node {$\bar{x}$};
\path (-2.2,0.24) node[rotate=90] {$P(\bar{X}=\bar{x})$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Find $P(\bar{X}\ge8)$.

(b) Find $E(\bar{X})$.
